\0
As the Freedom Guard won its first minor victories and demonstrated that they could challenge the Imperium, popular support for the rebellion spread quickly. Initially, the Freedom Guard armed forces were composed entirely of individuals from the Marked caste. But growing numbers of the common citizenry began to sympathize with the Freedom Guard cause and join in the struggle. Imperium troops attacked civilian populations across the planet Teron, where the first armed resistance had occurred centuries earlier, in an attempt to discourage support for the insurgents.
\1
Treasonous elements on a number of worlds are supporting the insurrection with supplies. We must not allow this seditious plague to take root in the general populace. We will give an example of the cost of defiance. Execution squads have been dispatched to several of Teron's major cities. Seize the planet's capitol, Ankara, and eliminate the seditious civilian element there.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
--> Establish a base in the city\n
--> Execute all rioting civilians\n
--> Cut off the Freedom Guard by destroying\n
\s\s\s\s all bridges around the city
\2
Your performance is adequate. Continue.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
The Imperium execution squad was intercepted by a Freedom Guard armored column on the outskirts of Ankara. Armed mainly with riot gear and anti-personnel weaponry, Imperium forces were poorly equipped to challenge the Freedom Guard armor and scattered into Ankara. Freedom Guard forces were able to sweep the city and dispatch the divided Imperium troops.\n\n
Several Imperium Guardians were pinned down and seized by a group of armed citizens. They were then beaten and dragged to the same courtyard where an Imperium regiment had executed an Exploratory Corps crew over 200 years earlier. The Guardians were bound between two Freedom Guard tanks and quartered.

